WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.611
Preflight checks confirm aircraft condition, propeller security, battery status,

00:00:03.611 --> 00:00:06.732
controller operation, navigation readiness, payload attachment, storage capacity,

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:07.903
and required settings.

00:00:07.903 --> 00:00:11.414
The crew should also verify the area, weather, communications,

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:13.754
and emergency plan immediately before launch.

00:00:13.754 --> 00:00:19.216
Maintain visual line of sight when required and operationally appropriate so the aircraft's position,

00:00:19.216 --> 00:00:22.337
orientation, flight path, and surrounding hazards remain understandable.

00:00:22.337 --> 00:00:26.239
A video feed narrows attention and may hide obstacles, people,

00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:28.969
or other aircraft outside the camera view.

00:00:28.969 --> 00:00:32.871
Situational awareness includes the aircraft, airspace, weather, crew, bystanders, vehicles,

00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:34.431
and changing ground conditions.

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:39.893
Establish safe distances and prevent unbriefed people from entering the launch or recovery area.

00:00:39.893 --> 00:00:43.404
Pause mission tasks when basic aircraft control needs attention.

00:00:43.404 --> 00:00:47.305
Loss of signal, unexpected navigation behavior, low battery, wind increase,

00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:50.036
and obstacle conflict require prompt conservative action.

00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:55.108
Follow the planned response and prioritize a safe landing over completing data collection.

00:00:55.108 --> 00:00:58.619
Automated behavior must be understood before it is needed.

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:02.130
Flyaway risk can be reduced through maintenance, configuration checks,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.861
current situational awareness, and appropriate operating limits,

00:01:04.861 --> 00:01:07.592
but it cannot be reduced to zero.

00:01:07.592 --> 00:01:12.664
Know how to warn the crew, protect people, record the last known information,

00:01:12.664 --> 00:01:15.395
and report an event through required channels.

00:01:15.395 --> 00:01:18.126
Crew communication should be brief and unambiguous.

00:01:18.126 --> 00:01:22.027
Call important hazards, battery thresholds, signal changes, and landing status.

00:01:22.027 --> 00:01:26.318
Any crew member should be able to raise a safety concern.

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:31.780
The pilot responsible for the flight must be willing to stop when margins disappear.
